    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Zurich Zebras is anchored by a high-upside trio of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.01), **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23), and **Christian Yelich** (75.84). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns the top spot against Teng due to a massive 14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup and the lead-off role, making him our primary target for stolen base accumulation. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core build-around; despite a neutral park, his elite 0.419 xwOBA and a strong platoon advantage against Rea ensure he remains a top-tier daily play. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from the soft matchup against Sasaki (5.11 xERA), with his 13% platoon boost elevating his potential to provide high-value run production from the cleanup spot.\n\nThe most critical tactical advantage on the board today involves **Trea Turner** (69.64). While wind blowing in at the stadium suppresses his raw score by 5%, his status as the leadoff hitter and his ability to weaponize the 100% stolen base opportunity against Cecconi\u2019s slow delivery keeps his floor extremely high. We are also monitoring **Casey Schmitt** (50.65) closely; he sits at the bottom of our start threshold. While his 11% platoon penalty against the lefty Hudson, B is painful, he was forced into the lineup over bench options like **Junior Caminero**\u2014who was sidelined by a rainout\u2014and the currently unavailable **Caleb Durbin** or **Hyeseong Kim**. The optimizer prioritized the consistency of **Casey Schmitt**\u2019s spot in the order over the volatility of unconfirmed depth pieces like **Colt Keith** or **Zac Veen**. \n\nManagers should remain wary of the weather impact on **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** (64.88), as the inward-blowing wind effectively caps their home run ceiling for the evening. We are keeping **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** on high alert should any late-inning defensive switches or injury substitutions become necessary, particularly given the weather-related risks lingering for the night slate. While **Gary Sanchez** (57.65) and **Luke Raley** (54.53) are in the lineup, they remain marginal plays that depend heavily on their ability to capitalize on the weak 5.11 xERA of Sasaki.",
